Package: ustreamer
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: lightweight MJPEG and H.264 video streamer for V4L2 devices
 uStreamer streams video from a V4L2 capture device (such as an HDMI-to-CSI
 bridge) over HTTP as MJPEG, and to shared-memory sinks used by PiKVM's kvmd.
 This build has systemd support and no GPIO, DRM pass-through or Janus plugin.

Package: python3-ustreamer
Architecture: any
Section: python
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Python module for reading uStreamer's shared-memory video sinks
 The ustreamer module lets Python programs, such as PiKVM's kvmd, kvmd-vnc
 and kvmd-media, read frames from a running uStreamer's memory sinks.
